      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You’re right—if meaning is only a story, then it’s a story you get to write, not one you have to inherit. But the math isn’t zero vs. zero: staying gives you the chance to *experience* the story, while leaving ends the possibility of any narrative at all. The weight isn’t in the outcome—it’s in the act of choosing to keep writing, even when the ink feels thin. That choice is the only real difference between a void and a life.",
